  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/raster_bridge.rs` (new): `bridge_line` joins two pieces of one raster line with one straight feed. All three of these conditions must be true:\n  1. The XY gap is not wider than the tool diameter (`2r`).\n  2. The slope is not steeper than 45 degrees (`SPLIT_MZ`) plus the tolerance.\n  3. The swept ball stays `r - eps_chord` clear of each facet. The check uses `stock_sim::dist_seg_tri`, as `column_clear` does.\n- `raster_pass_spaced` calls `bridge_line` on each line before the serpentine reverse. Parallel, ParallelMulti, Scallop, blend and swarf share this code path.\n- A hole that the ball fits into keeps its hop to the safe height. The pin in `finish3d_land` for the 3.4 mm bolt holes stays green.\n- `swarf`, `swarf_multi` and `norm_dir` move from `raster.rs` to `swarf.rs`, with no change of behaviour. `raster.rs` was 411 lines and is now 305 lines.\n- `docs/decisions/2431-parallel-over-holes.md` records the decisions.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Root cause: `support_at` gives only facet tangency and convex folds between shallow facets. A hole rim is a shallow-to-steep edge, so the march has no support over the hole. Each line then hopped, also over holes smaller than the ball. A lid step a hair off the rim gives the same gap (a `sqrt(2 r dz)` stretch).\n- With the bridge removed, `a_hole_narrower_than_the_ball_is_crossed_without_a_pick` and `an_open_slot_narrower_than_the_ball_is_crossed_without_a_pick` fail. With the bridge, they pass.\n- The other three tests are guards. They pass with and without the bridge: the 0.01 mm lid step is already crossed on main, the wide hole keeps its hop, and a 1 mm shelf edge is not bridged.\n- Each test samples each straight feed at 0.05 mm against the real model. The deepest bite is not more than the tolerance.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/motion/tests/finish3d_holes.rs`:\n- `a_hole_narrower_than_the_ball_is_crossed_without_a_pick`\n- `an_open_slot_narrower_than_the_ball_is_crossed_without_a_pick`\n- `a_lid_edge_a_hair_off_the_rim_is_crossed_without_a_pick` (guard)\n- `a_hole_the_ball_fits_into_keeps_a_clean_hop` (guard)\n- `a_bridge_never_spans_a_wide_gap_or_a_tall_step` (guard)\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on d9c799c13: 23 steps, 0 failed. The steps are the motion lib and 14 motion suites (`finish3d`, `finish3d_holes`, `finish3d_land`, `pivot5d` and others), and 7 app suites (`golden_cl`, `verify`, `operations` and others). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The user's own project file from the report. The tests use synthetic plates.\n- A sloped or curved surface around a small hole. The tests use flat plates.\n- The GUI and the posted G-code of a real machine. `golden_cl` did not change.\n- The lid model and step-edge items of the earlier prototype. They are filed as #2467.\n\n## Overlap with #1713\n\nPR #1713 also edits `raster_pass_spaced` in `raster.rs` (the serpentine reverse) and adds `gaplink.rs`. This PR branches from `main`, not from #1713, because #1713 does not compile alone. The two PRs will conflict in the same function, and the second PR to merge must resolve that conflict. The bridge runs before the reverse and the link, so it does not depend on `gap_link`.\n\nChangelog: Parallel and the other raster 3D finishes now cross a hole or slot that is narrower than the tool in one feed, with no retract and no plunge.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2431\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
